      "writtenOn": "2024-10-01T02:07:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the comment. These are very good questions. (1) The time for Bluetooth initiate connection to system start display is around 3s. I changed the time to 5s to give some buffer time. The wakelock should be released when the system resumes, or if the connection fails, and there are no input events, the wakelock should be released on timeout. (2) The wakelock is tracked by WakelockManager class and stats are saved as well. If there is a failure or duplicate lock acquire/release, they are also logged. I can add additional Bluetooth log when the lock is acqurie/release.",
      "parentUuid": "6e8e4bb1_a09bdb89",
